WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>My memories of that time are vague and murky.</i>

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.840
<i>My life felt like stagnant water.</i>

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.410
<i>I grew more and more impatient,</i>

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>but everything felt tiresome.</i>

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.830
<i>I wanted to take a step 
forward, but I was scared.</i>

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.280
<i>But...</i>

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>This pain in my chest,</i>

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>this agony...</i>

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:43.010
The Faraway Paladin

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:48.960
A long, long time ago, at the 
very beginning of the world,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.590
the mana that made up the world 
was too great to hold its shape,

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:55.630
and it swirled in a muddy mass of chaos.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.950
Then the first of the gods appeared.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.760
The god said, "Let there be earth,"

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.420
and the mana solidified beneath the 
god's feet, becoming the earth.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.250
The mana overhead thinned and became the sky.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.340
Hey, Gus, all I asked was how 
words are related to magic.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.500
Be quiet and listen!

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.860
I'm not even getting paid to 
teach you all this, you know!

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.180
Fine.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.820
The creator god made the sun and the moon,

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.050
and separated the land from the sea.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.200
Fire, wind, and trees came next,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.180
followed by other gods as 
well as humans and animals.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:30.030
<i>Gus the ghost is a little eccentric, 
and he can be overbearing,</i>

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.030
The creator god was pleased and said, "It is good."

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:34.070
<i>but he's smarter than anyone else, 
and he teaches me things.</i>

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.070
But good cannot exist without bad,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.470
and evil gods then came into being.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:40.660
And the words and symbols—in other words, 
writing—that the creator god used

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.580
are called the Words of Creation.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.750
These words, whether spoken 
or written, have power.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.870
Power?

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.000
Yes.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.600
If you write the word "Ignis," 
it defines the existence of fire.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.720
And... Erasus!

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.460
Erasure

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.540
When followed by the word for 
"erasure," the fire is extinguished.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.970
That's what magic is.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.990
<i>The power of words...</i>

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.850
Magic...

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.370
The god of justice and lightning, Volt.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.450
The earth-mother, Mater.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.250
The god of fire and technology, Blaze.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.350
The god of wind and commerce, Whirl.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.090
The goddess of water and 
greenery, Rhea Silvia.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.970
The god of knowledge, Enlight.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.710
<i>Ancient words of magic 
offered up to the gods...</i>

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.890
<i>Words of Creation.</i>

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:52.150
Oh, I get it. Parts are scratched 
out so their powers won't activate.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.750
Gracefeel...

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.830
Are you curious?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.210
Yeah, sort of.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.200
The god of light, who governs 
the cycle of death and rebirth,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.500
Gracefeel.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.940
He is the child of the lightning god 
Volt and the earth-mother Mater.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.220
You worship the earth-mother Mater, right?

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.270
Yes, that's right.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.570
She is the god of child-rearing 
and the bounties of the earth.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.580
Of the six principal gods,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.570
she is particularly revered 
by people in rural areas.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:41.780
You pray to the earth-mother 
every day, don't you?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.700
Mary?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.200
Shall we head back and have dinner now?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.240
Yeah!

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.110
Blood!

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.630
That's a really nice boar!

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.100
You get to eat some tasty meat 
from this guy today, Will.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.790
Thanks!

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.730
Hey, that hurts.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.560
Wow, it looks so good!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.850
Eat up.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.490
I will!

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.320
It's great!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.280
Thanks, Blood! And you, too, Mary!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.530
That's right. Be grateful.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.560
Once you're a little bigger, 
I'll teach you how to hunt.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.290
What? Hunt?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.000
Hunting teaches you all kinds of lessons.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.670
You're gonna have to get 
used to taking lives.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.960
What's the matter? Losing your nerve?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.050
He's still too young for that!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.290
That's right.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.600
He needs to learn the basics first.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.440
I couldn't believe it.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.450
He's only three, and he's already 
learned to read and write.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:56.400
He might be just as much a genius as me.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.100
It couldn't hurt to teach him some magic.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.450
Hey, give us a break!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:05.600
What if he grows up to be an old miser 
with an over sized brain, like you?

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:08.410
<i>Blood the skeleton looks scary, 
and he can be unruly,</i>

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.320
What?!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.120
What Will needs is some muscle!

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.470
We gotta put some meat on his bones first!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.660
but he always keeps things 
lively and friendly.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.660
What are you talking about?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.990
Also, the "miser" part aside, 
what was that about an over sized brain?

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.120
Hey, Mary...

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.460
What's wrong with strengthening 
the body, anyway?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.630
When do you bake this bread?

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.630
Oh, just shut up!

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.380
That's a secret.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.510
<i>The three of them keep a lot of secrets.</i>

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.820
<i>Like why they live here,</i>

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.760
<i>and why there are no humans other than me.</i>

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.830
<i>I've never met anyone but the 
three of them since I was born.</i>

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:38.770
<i>And above all...</i>

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.510
<i>Why are they undead?</i>

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:46.650
<i>There are so many things I 
want to ask them, but I can't.</i>

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.600
<i>Because I'm keeping a 
secret from them myself.</i>

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.800
<i>And that is...</i>

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.520
Thanks for dinner!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.240
<i>...that I'm a human with 
memories of my previous life.</i>

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.890
<i>They're vague, murky memories,</i>

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.750
<i>and my vision won't focus...</i>

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.070
<i>A ceiling?</i>

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.230
<i>A monster!</i>

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:27.360
<i>A mummy?!</i>

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.360
<i>A ghost?!</i>

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.350
<i>They're gonna kill me!</i>

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.030
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.510
<i>This is the 186th morning since then,</i>

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:52.510
<i>half a year since I started living 
with these walking corpses.</i>

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.980
Time to eat.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.860
What a good boy you are, Will.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.240
Are you all full now?

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.940
<i>I can't say them very well,</i>

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.450
<i>but I can generally understand 
the language they speak now.</i>

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.700
Shall we take a little walk outside today?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:22.580
<i>Outside? I've never been outside before!</i>

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:27.960
<i>It smells like incense.</i>

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.820
<i>What's it like outside the temple?</i>

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.020
<i>The breeze was refreshing.</i>

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.800
<i>It smelled of the plants, 
wet with morning dew.</i>

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.240
Isn't it beautiful, Will?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.530
<i>It really was beautiful.</i>

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.370
It's all right.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.330
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.580
<i>At first, I thought I'd fallen into Hell.</i>

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:10.060
<i>After living such a hopelessly vague life,</i>

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:12.840
<i>I was in Hell, being punished.</i>

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.970
<i>But I was wrong. This is no punishment.</i>

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.300
<i>It must be...</i>

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.850
<i>the grace of God.</i>

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.580
<i>I felt as if something I had wastefully 
thrown away without a thought</i>

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.210
<i>had been given back to me again.</i>

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:31.110
Will, my sweet little boy...

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.490
<i>This time... This time...</i>

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.530
<i>I'm going to live.</i>

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.040
<i>I'm going to live in this world.</i>

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.750
<i>Finally done...</i>

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.970
We gotta build your muscle and stamina first.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.800
Skills are useless without 
the muscle to back 'em up.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.640
Isn't making up for your 
lack of strength a skill?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.390
Think you can knock me down?

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.700
No.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.640
With the right skill, 
you could knock me over,

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.080
but there'll be times when 
that skill won't work for you.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.640
But you can't separate 
muscles from your body.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:12.070
The brute force that muscles give 
you can solve most problems.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.650
Skills come after that.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.290
Understand?

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.280
Muscles are super masochistic, huh?

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.080
Flammo Ignis!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.750
Flames Ignite

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.330
Erasus!

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.320
Erasure

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.050
Fool! Your pronunciation is too precise!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.710
Given your talent, you need to 
learn to control your accuracy,

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.050
or you will kill yourself!

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.020
That's scary...

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.390
Magic is a scary thing.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:44.270
Do you know why words have so much power?

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.610
I think it's for the same reason we 
think a chair is "a chair," right?

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.520
Indeed.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.940
When we see a wooden stool with four legs,

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:56.450
no matter what color it is or 
what kind of wood it's made of,

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.100
we don't think of it as 
"four sticks and a round slab,"

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.660
nor would we call it a "table."

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.060
We categorize it under the "chair" label.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:10.210
So in short, words are what define 
and differentiate the way things are.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.090
<i>I'm just repeating what 
someone told me, though.</i>

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.620
Hmm...

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.660
Will, you might just be a genius after all.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.760
But isn't there anything I can 
do about my mixed results?

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.840
No! That is what words are all about.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.310
Words have fluctuations.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:29.650
No one can say a word in 
exactly the same way twice.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.290
The only answer is to let your 
instincts determine the ideal level.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.570
My instincts?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:39.420
You'll start by learning how to use 
minor magic skillfully and accurately.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.350
But do your best to get by 
without even using that.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.870
Without using magic? How?

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.580
I'm talking about money.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.130
That again?

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.790
How can a ghost be such a money worshiper?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.740
What are you talking about? 
Money is important!

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:56.200
Money drives this world!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.670
With the power of money, you can 
solve anything without magic!

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:02.260
You can buy the necessary 
tools, hire people...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:07.350
The ability to make a quick profit 
is just as important as magic!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:12.190
Why, oh, why must I have hands that are 
incapable of stroking silver and gold?!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.400
I want to feel money! I want to 
count gold coins with my own hands!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.550
Curses!

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.780
You are not normal...

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.530
Creatures such as these are "beasts."

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:29.290
"Demon beasts" are a particular type 
of beast that are extremely aggressive.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.290
That's...

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.000
Old Gus taught you the myths, right?

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.170
The minions of the god 
of despotism and tyranny,

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.820
spectres and phantoms...

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:43.780
and the demons of the god of 
dimensions, who lurks in Hell.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:48.770
And the god of the undead, 
Stagnate, commands undead.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.640
People like the three of us.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.080
We used to be humans, as well.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.710
What? Really?

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:57.780
Yes.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.410
When we died, we clung to 
powerful emotions that led us

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.910
to form a contract with 
the god of the undead.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.780
We are traitors to the virtuous gods.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:08.800
Mary...

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:14.000
I'm sorry for talking 
about such strange things.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.630
Hey, Mary, do you think 
I should get stronger?

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.300
It would certainly put me at ease if you did.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.350
Don't make it suffer.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:35.850
Snap its neck quick.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.440
Still can't get used to it, huh?

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:47.480
I don't like killing.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.200
Am I just naïve?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.370
Hey, I don't like it, either.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.290
Huh?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.580
I don't like taking lives, 
whether it's a bird's or a human's.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:58.960
But these guys are necessary 
sustenance to keep you alive.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:04.310
In life-or-death situations, you put all 
that aside and go for the kill reflexively.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.340
That's what it means to be a warrior.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.390
In battle, it determines 
whether you live or die.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.850
Okay, let's bring down a few more.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.100
Okay.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.160
<i>Blood seems a lot like a father.</i>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.280
You're almost eight years old.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.240
I think it's time you started 
some real-life training.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.530
What?

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.140
It's bad enough when you 
stop just before hitting me.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:31.200
If I take a hit with your 
ridiculous strength, I'm dead!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.710
I'm nothing but bones now.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.750
You'll be fine... probably.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.720
Probably?!

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.530
This is why I said you can use the 
magic you're learning from the old man!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.960
Go on. Do just as I taught you.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.300
That's right. Do it well, 
and you could actually hit me...

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.460
Maybe!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.510
Hey!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.680
And don't cry that I'm playing dirty!

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.140
The battle has begun!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.060
Acceleratio!

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:52.960
Accelerate

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:55.430
Currere!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:55.130
Run

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.230
Oleum!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.130
Oil

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.810
Cadere Araneum!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.600
Falling Spiderweb

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.400
Hey, not too shabby!

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.290
Fool! Distance yourself!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.460
C'mon. I told you never to 
close your eyes during a fight.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.220
Ow!

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:23.800
I'd like to say you've got a long way 
to go, but frankly, you surprised me.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.050
I thought you'd unload a 
bunch of crazy magic on me.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:31.850
Gus keeps telling me I should learn to use 
minor magic skillfully and accurately.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.650
That style of not relying on sheer firepower

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:39.720
is exactly the style of the great 
sorcerer hailed as the Wandering Sage.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.360
Are you talking about Gus?

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.410
Yep.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:45.760
He's exterminated monsters, 
calmed raging rivers,

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.220
and rediscovered ancient languages.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.110
Hmph. That was long ago.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:53.380
You were known as the War Ogre yourself.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.720
And Mary was known as the Daughter of Mater.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.450
At one time, the three of us...

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.370
Wow!

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.650
Never mind.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.380
That subject runs a little too deep.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.530
Not long ago, you were just a little baby.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.590
Keep up your learning and get even stronger.

00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:11.400
Blood...

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:14.080
When you brought back a human child,

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.470
I thought you shouldn't have bothered,

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:20.080
but it occurred to me that if I 
educated him, he might be of use—

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:20.980
Hey, old man!

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.360
Nothing I said was incorrect!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.610
I now recognize his talent and 
am teaching him, am I not?!

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:28.990
That's not the point.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.240
I know that's just how you are.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.210
I don't expect you to change that now.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.880
I even think it suits you.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:39.870
But what you just said was unnecessary.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.760
Can't you imagine how it feels to 
be the one on the other end of it?

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:47.310
You are right. It was a 
thoughtless thing to say.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.510
I will be more careful in the future.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.890
I apologize, Will.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:54.630
Oh, it's okay. It didn't bother me.

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:56.100
<i>I couldn't believe it.</i>

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.100
<i>Gus was apologizing?</i>

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.980
It was rude of me to get all 
intimidating like that, too.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.060
Sorry.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.790
You being impolite is nothing new.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.070
What?!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.440
Will...

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:12.270
You might not realize it since it's been

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:15.320
this way for as long as you've been aware,

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:19.450
but you know that you're not 
like the three of us, right?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.540
Yeah.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:24.040
I'm the only one who breathes and feels warm.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:28.300
Yeah, basically. There's a lot to the story.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:31.610
Sorry, though. I can't explain it to you yet.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.570
I know.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:35.580
Don't be too mad at Old Gus.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:40.340
He never bothers to choose his 
words or show consideration.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:43.810
I'm not mad. I respect Gus.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:44.990
That so?

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.070
You've got a big heart.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:51.920
Once your body's grown big 
enough to match that heart

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:56.160
and you're able to accept things, 
I'll explain everything.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.030
Okay.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.390
<i>Blood was genuinely angry at him for my sake.</i>

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:07.430
<i>Could I have gotten angry for someone 
else's sake in my previous life?</i>

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:12.760
Thanks.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.540
<i>Blood, Mary, Gus...</i>

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.840
<i>All three of them are undead 
who aren't alive anymore...</i>

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.760
Will...

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.870
You've got another hundred years before you

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:24.310
can land a hit on me from behind!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.800
H-Huh?!

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:29.090
<i>But right now, they're my precious family.</i>

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:36.150
<i>Gus teaches me academic lessons, 
and Blood teaches me how to fight,</i>

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:39.060
<i>but Mary is the one I learn the most from.</i>

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.950
<i>The things she teaches me are 
little, everyday matters,</i>

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.620
<i>but they're important.</i>

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.650
Will, can you take care of things here?

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.150
Oh, it's almost time for 
your prayer, isn't it?

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:48.960
Yes.

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:53.440
<i>A few times a day, Mary sequesters 
herself inside the temple dome.</i>

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:58.210
<i>I've been told I'm not allowed to 
go in the dome while she's in there.</i>

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.470
All right, it's time for 
your physical training.

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.930
I can't lift my arms...

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:10.210
Mary?

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.300
<i>Bread?</i>

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.840
<i>Why is she carrying it out of the temple?</i>

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.570
When do you bake this bread?

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.950
That's a secret.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.660
<i>I'm sorry, everyone,</i>

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.040
<i>but I just have to know.</i>

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:43.970
Ma—

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:46.730
<i>No...</i>

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:48.390
<i>I don't want to feel that again...</i>

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:51.820
<i>I don't want to lose anyone again!</i>

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.070
Mary!

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:56.940
Mary!

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.010
Mary! Mary!

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:00.770
Mary!

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.660
Blood! Gus! Come in here!

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.250
Help Mary... Help Mary!

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.630
It's...

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.380
It's all my fault.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.880
I kept it a secret...

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.190
Sorry. I was careless.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.680
All those times we told him to be careful...

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.630
Will his arms heal?

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:26.080
Thankfully, his fingers 
didn't adhere to each other,

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.310
but scarring will be unavoidable.

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:29.930
Mary...

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:33.380
Will! I'm sorry... This is my...

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:37.140
No, it's not. It's my fault for prying.

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.010
So don't apologize.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.070
I'm glad you're all right.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.600
Will...

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:48.540
<i>The smell of incense that Mary has calms me.</i>

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.430
Why'd you try to look in on her?

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:53.910
I got curious.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:57.370
I thought I might find some hint about

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:59.800
what you guys are hiding from me.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.800
I told you I'd explain someday.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.630
Blood!

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.240
Be quiet, Mary.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.060
Well, Will? Want to give me an excuse?

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:10.400
No. I'm sorry.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:14.090
From now on, consult with me 
or Mary before doing anything.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.000
Okay.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.110
That said, Will,

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.740
the way you jumped in there 
to help Mary was impressive.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:21.390
Those wounds you bear are 
your badge of manhood.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.990
Well, I'm your student.

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.620
All it got you was unnecessarily 
wounded, though.

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:30.660
Well, out of respect for your lack of fear 
toward the fire, I'll teach you this.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.960
That bread is a gift from 
the earth-mother Mater.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:39.310
They are the goddess's divine protection, 
her blessing... call it what you will.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.260
Then why were you on fire?

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.330
That happens because I betrayed 
the earth-mother Mater.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:51.020
The impure god of death, Stagnate, 
is the earth-mother Mater's enemy.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.770
Since the three of us formed 
a contract with him,

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:57.880
just coming in contact with her 
divine presence causes us to burn.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.270
That's awful...

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:01.650
I do not expect to be forgiven.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.990
Why do you still pray to her?

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.240
For my sake?

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.490
No, Will.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.810
Praying to the earth-mother 
every morning and evening

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:15.120
has been my daily routine 
since long before I met you.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.590
Doesn't it hurt?

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:19.490
Of course it does. So badly that I could cry.

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:20.610
Mary...

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.630
But even if I've betrayed her, 
even if I must endure pain in retribution,

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:29.390
I still continue to revere the earth-mother.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:31.890
Mater never says anything,

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:35.490
but she blesses me with 
bread for you every day.

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:38.960
That alone is more than 
enough saving grace for me.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.470
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:45.930
I hope you will continue to eat the bread.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:48.400
Yes, I will.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.780
Also, I want to ask a favor.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:52.100
What is it?

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:55.030
From now on, let me pray with you.

00:21:55.930 --> 00:22:01.920
<i>I want to understand what Mary sees 
and feels, even if only a little bit.</i>

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:04.910
Episode 1
The Boy from the City of the Dead

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.050
<i>That was the thought I had.</i>

00:23:35.430 --> 01:00:00.000
Episode 2
The Wandering Sage
